 "title": "Verticillium dahliae Pathogenicity and Protein Expression",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the pathogenic fungus Verticillium dahliae and its interactions with various organisms and chemicals. V. dahliae has pathogenicity towards Cotton and expresses several proteins, including AAs, CAZymes, CBMs, CEs, G2WZT4, and SCRPs. The fungus also has a relationship with the gene VdMFS2, which is expressed in Cotton and is used as a host for the organism Vd592. Additionally, VdMFS2 is used as a vector for the method pTRV2-00 and is silenced by the method HIGS. The cluster also includes various mutants and organisms related to V. dahliae, such as ΔVdMFS2-4 and ΔVdMFS2-4Y.",
